      <para id="para-00005">Algebra 1 by OpenStax is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License v4.0. Algebra 1 was authored by OpenStax and is based, in part, on OpenStax Prealgebra, Elementary Algebra, Intermediate Algebra, and College Algebra materials, and the IM 6–12 Math™ by Illustrative Mathematics®.</para>
      <para id="para-00006">
<media alt="Logo of OpenStax with a stack of five horizontal, colorful bars in green, orange, gray, yellow, and blue on the left and the text &quot;openstax&quot; on the right.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_01_01_06.png" width="300px"/>
          </media>

<media alt="Textbook cover image with dark green background and large yellow text reading 'Algebra 1.' Below, a yellow bar contains the smaller text 'K12 Curriculum.'">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_00_01_01_07.png" width="170"/>
          </media>

    </para>
      <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Senior Contributing Authors:</title>
      <list bullet-style="none" id="list-00001">
        <item><emphasis>Lynn Marecek, Santa Ana College</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>MaryAnne Anthony-Smith, Formerly of Santa Ana College</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>Andrea Honeycutt Mathis, Northeast Mississippi Community College</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>Jay Abramson, Arizona State University</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>Sharon North, St. Louis Community College</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>Amy Baldwin, University of Central Arkansas</emphasis></item>
        <item><emphasis>Alyssa Howell, OpenStax, Rice University</emphasis></item>
      </list>
      </section>
      <para id="para-00007">Algebra 1 was authored by OpenStax and is based, in part, on the OpenStax Prealgebra, Elementary Algebra, Intermediate Algebra, and College Algebra materials, and the IM 6–12 Math™ by Illustrative Mathematics®. Based on OpenStax’s open (CC-BY) license, educators may remix and reuse the elements and content in Algebra 1 according to their approach. OpenStax textbooks are always free online.</para>
      <section id="sect-00003"><title>Errata</title>
      <para id="para-00008">All OpenStax textbooks undergo a rigorous review process. However, like any professional-grade textbook, errors sometimes occur. If you have a correction to suggest, submit it to k12@openstax.org. We review your suggestions and make the necessary changes.</para></section>

      <para id="para-00009">Students who don’t complete Algebra 1 have just a 1 in 5 chance of graduating from high school. Increasing access to rigorous, engaging, standards-aligned Algebra content helps prepare more students to succeed in higher-level mathematics.</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>Algebra 1 is a critical “gateway course” in K12 education.</item>
        <item>Success in Algebra 1 is a predictor of on-time graduation rates, success in higher-level mathematics, and post-secondary success.</item>
        <item>OpenStax Algebra 1 is a High-Quality Instructional Material designed for secondary Algebra instruction.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00010">OpenStax Algebra 1 is a complete Algebra 1 curriculum and an open education resource (OER) that is standards-aligned, easy to implement, supportive of diverse learners, and engaging for students. Algebra 1 is supported by instructional support resources, including implementation guidance, pacing suggestions, and ancillary engagement materials.</para>
      <para id="para-00011">ISBN: 978-1-961584-47-1<newline/>
            E-book, digital online<newline/>
            Publication date: February 1, 2023</para>
